  "name": "Rheumatoid Factor (RA Qualitative)",
  "code": "RA Q",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The qualitative rheumatoid factor (RF) test is used to detect the presence or absence of RF antibodies in the blood. Here is an interpretation of the qualitative RF test:<br></p><ul><li><p>Negative: If the RF test result is negative, it indicates that RF antibodies are not detectable in the blood. This is considered normal and suggests a lower likelihood of rheumatoid arthritis (RA) or other autoimmune conditions associated with RF positivity.</p></li><li><p>Positive: If the RF test result is positive, it indicates the presence of RF antibodies in the blood. However, it is important to note that a positive RF test alone is not diagnostic of any specific condition. RF antibodies can be found in various autoimmune diseases, including rheumatoid arthritis, but can also be present in healthy individuals or individuals with other non-autoimmune conditions.</p></li></ul>",
